person  In SolidWorks, open the Reducer_12to1.SLDASM a section built (a2 or m4). Click gear G1 — the small gear on S1, at the origin — and drag it round its axis by about a quarter turn. Watch G4, the large gear on S3: it turns the same way as G1, much more slowly — a quarter turn of G1 turns G4 about 7.5°. G2 and G3, on S2, turn together the other way. No gear should leave its axis, slide along it, or pass through another. Then, in the Workbook window, press Update SolidWorks with nothing changed: the footer should say the gears stand where they were turned. Tell us what you saw, on each version.
